# ZKM's reviewed, default-deny public source policy.
#
# IN: exact source, reproducibility metadata, protocol documentation, and
# deterministic checkers required for the minimal reference snapshot. Public
# projections replace the scanner-incompatible family consumer files below.
# OUT: open-source overlay material, private CI, proving output, proof or
# witness fixtures, website assets, benchmarks, economics, and internal plans.
# The AFP-KDC conformance vector and its checker are also excluded: the trusted
# exporter scanner flags deterministic values in that vector as generic API
# keys and accepts no caller- or repository-specific exceptions. Their direct
# consumer metadata is supplied only by scanner-clean overlay projections; the
# canonical private files are not redacted or modified.
# The source-specific Aztec README is excluded because it contains private
# operational tracking metadata; no source redaction is performed here.
# Every entry below is one exact tracked regular file; directories and globs
# are intentionally not policy syntax.
